  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q7",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "A circle has centre $(4,-3)$ and one of the $x$-intercepts is at $(-\\sqrt{7}+4,0)$. Determine the equation of the circle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(x-4)^2+(y+3)^2=16$",
      "worked": "The radius is the distance from the centre to the intercept.\n$$\\begin{align*}r&=\\sqrt{(4-\\sqrt{7}-4)^2+(0+3)^2}\\\\&=\\sqrt{7+9}\\\\&=4\\end{align*}$$\nWith centre $(4,-3)$ and radius $4$:\n$$(x-4)^2+(y+3)^2=16.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 23
